2317|v|To consider by turning a subject in the mind, and viewing it in its different aspects and relations; to meditate; to contemplate; to theorize; as, to speculate on questions in religion; to speculate on political events. ; To view subjects from certain premises given or assumed, and infer conclusions respecting them a priori. ; To purchase with the expectation of a contingent advance in value, and a consequent sale at a profit; -- often, in a somewhat depreciative sense, of unsound or hazardous transactions; as, to speculate in coffee, in sugar, or in bank stock. ; To consider attentively; as, to speculate the nature of a thing.	d:s3j,17,10;2l6,5,6~s3j,17,10;2l6,5,6	D:29qk,12,3;10ln,10,3~29qk,12,3;10ln,10,3
